; --cost with a priced posting among conversion postings: which pairs go (see conversion.md for
; the postings that balance by their quantity)
2026-01-01 a matching pair: the priced posting balances by quantity, the pair goes
    a  2 X @ 3 EUR
    equity:conversion  -2 X
    equity:conversion  6 EUR
    b  -6 EUR

2026-01-02 a pair that matches nothing: the priced posting balances by cost, the first posting without a price is unique
    a  2 X @ 3 EUR
    b  -6 EUR
    equity:conversion  -1 EUR
    equity:conversion  1 EUR

2026-01-03 the only other posting is priced: no anchor, the pair stays
    a  2 X @ 1 EUR
    equity:trading  4 EUR
    equity:trade  -6 EUR

2026-01-04 one conversion posting opens the transaction and the priced posting balances by quantity: the pair goes
    equity:conversion  -3 X
    a  3 X @ 2 EUR
    equity:conversion  1 EUR
    equity:conversion  1 EUR
    b  -2 EUR

2026-01-05 the same, but c repeats the quantity, so it balances by cost: nothing goes
    equity:conversion  -3 X
    a  3 X @ 2 EUR
    equity:conversion  1 EUR
    equity:conversion  1 EUR
    b  -8 EUR
    c  3 X

2026-01-06 three conversion postings open the transaction, balance by cost: nothing goes
    equity:conversion  1 EUR
    equity:conversion  1 EUR
    equity:conversion  -3 X
    a  3 X @ 2 EUR
    b  -8 EUR
    c  3 X

2026-01-07 the lone conversion posting does not open the transaction, by cost: the pair goes
    b  -12 EUR
    equity:conversion  -3 X
    a  3 X @@ 6 EUR
    equity:conversion  -3 X
    equity:conversion  6 EUR
    c  6 X
